    {
      "jobId": "8120bb8d-e660-48ea-a488-c2b3ef4ba25e",
      "question": "How many stocks are in each SIC division, and what was each division's median return from January 2 to March 12, 2026?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-02T16:53:45.701502Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-02T16:55:11.952939Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "| SIC Division | Stock Count | Median Return |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Manufacturing | 579 | –1.22% |\n| Finance, Insurance and Real Estate | 363 | –1.50% |\n| Services | 264 | –12.50% |\n| Transportation, Communications and Utilities | 99 | +3.81% |\n| Nonclassifiable | 89 | –3.37% |\n| Retail Trade | 83 | –4.05% |\n| Mining | 64 | +20.70% |\n| Wholesale Trade | 40 | +2.07% |\n| Agriculture, Forestry and Fishing | 10 | +9.09% |\n| Construction | 10 | –3.49% |\n\n[1]\n\n**Notes**\n- Returns are measured per stock from its last close before 2026‑01‑02 (or its first close in the window if it listed later) to its last close on or before 2026‑03‑12. Stocks without a close in the window are excluded from the median but still counted in the division total.\n- The data pack covers daily prices from 2025‑01‑02 through 2026‑03‑12.\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Structured retrieval result — us_equities — evidence `hermes-receipt:ca34da629ffe12ca9e1b02dbfaca44da718e5d7fc50c8c4c9b3969145599f58c`",
